**Project**: Rail Runner (轨道跑者) — 2.5D isometric infinite runner

**Why**: Build a playable prototype fast, validate core loop, then consider Godot migration at Tier 3+.

**How to apply**: When working on this project, read `production/session-state/active.md` first. The game is a single-file `src/index.html` (~1225 lines). No build system, no dependencies. Open in browser to test.

## Current State (2026-05-20)

- **Stage**: Tier 1 core loop — playable prototype
- **Engine**: Web Canvas (HTML5 Canvas 2D + vanilla JavaScript)
- **Game code**: `src/index.html` (~1225 lines, ~55KB)
- **Design doc**: `design/gdd/game-concept.md`
- **Tech config**: `.claude/docs/technical-preferences.md` (updated to Web Canvas)

## What's Implemented
- 2.5D perspective projection (`worldToScreen`, `laneX`)
- 3-lane track system with smooth lane switching
- Player states: run, jump, slide, hit
- 3 obstacle types: low (slide under), mid (jump over), high (lane-switch required)
- Coin collection with particle effects
- 3-heart health system with invincibility frames
- Progressive difficulty (speed increases, obstacle mix changes)
- Score = distance + coins, high score persisted to localStorage
- Object pooling (obstacles, coins, particles)
- Offscreen pre-rendering (sky, buildings, player sprites, obstacle sprites, coin sprite)
- Parallax scrolling cityscape (2 layers)
- Keyboard + touch input (swipe detection)
- Start screen, death screen, HUD (hearts, score, speed %)

